## Method

`reference/*/gen` is gitignored, so the enumeration's "pre-existing" verdict
rested on a mechanism argument. It is now settled by regeneration: all six
failures were first reproduced with the scoped run at `ec4c5c2d`, then the five
relevant trees (ts, rust, rust-f32, kotlin, swift, dart) were regenerated fresh
with `haxe examples/<target>.hxml` (all exit 0) and **all six failures
reproduced on the fresh output** — none is a stale-tree artifact.
`evidence/baseline-six-fails.log` (exit 1, 6 fails / 88 pass).

Each red was then adjudicated by the project's own discrimination: compare the
fresh generated form against what the Haxe source declares, and date the
expectation's pin against the generator behavior it describes.

## Per-failure rulings

### 1. arithmetic helpers — Rust inlining — EXPECTATION STALE (refreshed, stronger)

The pin `return (value) >= (low) && (value) <= (high);` was written
`ad3bbc2f` 2026-08-28; the signed-domain comparison rule
(`SignedBusinessComparison`, from `8eef922f` 2026-09-25) post-dates it. Haxe
`Int` is signed; the business u32 rendering reinterprets both operands to i32
(`i32::from_ne_bytes`) before comparing, with an explicit rationale and
counterexample (an empty `IntRange 0..-1` would compare `0 > -1` true under a
naive u32 compare). The generated form preserves the declared semantics —
refreshed the pin to the full reinterpreted statements (within, clampLeast,
clampMost, inRange). Strictly stronger: pins inlining AND the signed domain;
the `not.toContain("Arithmetic::")` guards are unchanged.

### 2. RustExpr.hx banned identifier — GENERATOR WRONG (fixed)

16 `#if boring_fold_debug` gates named the compiled package. The boundary
precedent is the identical Kotlin violation fixed by renaming
(`7c1305ff`: `boring_fold_debug` -> `kotlin_fold_debug`); `KotlinExpr.hx`
reads `kotlin_fold_debug` today. Renamed to `rust_fold_debug`; no hxml/doc
references the old name (it was inactive), and `haxe examples/rust.hxml`
regenerates the rust tree **byte-identical** (diff -rq empty) — output-neutral.

Note (not fixed, out of scope): `SwiftExpr.hx` carries the same
`boring_fold_debug` name twice, but the boundary test's directory list does not
scan `swiftcompiler/`; `SwiftExpr.hx` also carried another agent's in-flight
patch at the time. Reported, not touched.

### 3. loop structure, reference/ts/gen — GENERATOR WRONG (fixed)

Six unhoisted for-heads (`for (let i0 = 0; i0 < a.fontFamilies.length && ...)`)
in `SortedDataClassKeysOps.ts`, `PrintedCollection.ts`, `GlyphClusterHolder.ts`,
all from the dataClass comparator emitter `TsDecl.hx` `Lexicographic`. The
feature-09 rule (restated in the test contract) requires the condition to
evaluate as a local, with the sanctioned hoist in the init section; these were
the only such heads in the fresh tree. Fixed: bind
`n<depth> = min(left.length, right.length)` in the init section.

### 4. loop structure, reference/rust/gen — GENERATOR WRONG (fixed)

Fresh-tree hits: `.map(` call-site files `runtime/env.rs`, `runtime/u_string.rs`,
`boring/platform_ops.rs`, `registry/main.rs` + one lambda-in-loop-body in
`boring/payload_text_table.rs`. All from compiler-side renderings that post-date
the guard (test `89d80488` 2026-08-26; emissions `2193c2df`/`5b3812f3`
2026-09-26, `d9a23f70`):

- `std.Process.args()` lowering -> new embedded-runtime helper
  `u_string::args_from_host()` collecting with a while loop (call sites
  platform_ops.rs, registry/main.rs re-imported).
- StringBuf add trail gate `.map_or(false, |head| ...)` -> `match` on
  `encode_utf16().next()` (same predicate, no lambda inside caller loops).
- Embedded runtime text (`RustRuntime.hx`): `Env::get`, `unit_at_from` (both
  variants), `unit_at`, `u_string_at` render `Option::map` as `match`;
  `u_string_to_code_points` renders `.iter().map().collect()` as an index loop.
  Semantics identical; `cargo check` exit 0 on both rust trees, `cargo test`
  exit 0 (16 passed) on reference/rust.

Note: the remaining `.map_or(false, |v| ...)` sites elsewhere in the tree are
outside loop bodies and contain no `.map(` substring — the scanner passes them
by construction, unchanged.

### 5. sorted dataClass keys — pins resident comparators — EXPECTATION STALE (refreshed)

Two stale layers, both masked behind the first failing assertion:

- Swift marker `func compareRubySpan`: the Swift target now names dataClass
  record comparators by source path (`compareRecord_6_boring_22_..._8_RubySpan`,
  `SwiftComparisonPlan.hx`, commit `4581308d` 2026-09-28 — after the test's
  `09a868fc` 2026-09-02). The comparator is still resident, bound at every
  `SortedTable.mapBuilder` call site, and its body still reads every declared
  field (fontFamilies, kind, locale) — the pinned property holds; refreshed to
  the exact current symbol, body assertions unchanged.
- PrintedEnum order helpers: off the TS target the enum order is no longer a
  named helper — Kotlin/Dart render the constructor-index `when`/`switch`
  inline at both comparison sites, Rust emits numbered order fns
  (`printed_badge_order_0`). Each still orders by declared constructor index.
  Refreshed to pins that name the comparator function and its ordering
  expression per target.

### 6. sorted key domains — Rust int capacity bound — EXPECTATION STALE (refreshed)

`set.size()` is a resident call returning the i32 domain; the
resident-to-business boundary now casts to u32 before the bit reinterpretation,
so the pinned substring lacked `(... as u32)`. The tested property — the usize
widening stays infallible (`usize::try_from(...).unwrap_or(0)`, no error enum,
no `map_err` path) — is intact in the fresh output. Refreshed to the exact
current statement; the `Vec::with_capacity(capacity)` pin is unchanged.

